    "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nFix MultiConnector initialization when a child connector explicitly sets `engine_id`.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Honor explicit child engine IDs and inherit the parent ID when omitted.\r\n- Preserve the original child configuration dictionaries.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- **31 passed, 2 deselected** for the unit-test selection below.\r\n- **1 passed, 32 deselected** for `test_multi_example_connector_consistency`, using the local `DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B` checkpoint instead of the gated Llama checkpoint. All test assertions were retained, including matching saved KV contents, first-connector cache reuse, and second-connector fallback after deleting the first store.\r\n- All applicable pre-commit hooks passed for all three changed files.\r\n\r\nBefore the fix, both the new unit regression and the same local-model integration scenario failed with:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nTypeError: vllm.config.kv_transfer.KVTransferConfig() got multiple values for keyword argument 'engine_id'\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnit-test command:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nHF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 uv run --no-sync .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\r\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_multi_connector.py -q \\\r\n  -k \"not multi_example_connector_consistency and not mixed_hma_disables_hybrid_kv_cache\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe integration test was run on one H800 in eager mode with `VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn`. A local pytest collection plugin changed only the test module's `MODEL_NAME` to the local checkpoint. The original gated-model configuration and the mixed-HMA test were not run.\r\n\r\nThe new regression is marked `cpu_test` so the existing CPU Buildkite lane selects it. Local `-m cpu_test` selection passed (1 passed, 32 deselected). The upstream GPU KV Connector step is currently disabled; upstream CI results for the new head are pending.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nPassing `engine_id` explicitly alongside `**ktc` caused a duplicate-keyword error when the child configuration already contained that key.\r\n\r\nMerge the parent default with the child configuration so an explicitly configured child `engine_id` takes precedence, while preserving the original configuration dictionary.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n\r\n</details>",
